---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy · Stillmic"
  description="What Stillmic does with your data."
>
  <main id="main" class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      Stillmic processes your microphone on your Mac. Your audio is never stored
      and never sent anywhere. There is no account and there are no analytics.
    </p>
    <h2>Microphone</h2>
    <p>
      Stillmic reads your real microphone only while another app is using the
      Stillmic mic.
    </p>
    <h2>Network</h2>
    <p>
      The app’s only network request is checking for updates, using
      <a href="https://sparkle-project.org">Sparkle</a>. That request goes to
      GitHub, which sees your IP address as it would for any download.
    </p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site has no cookies and no analytics. It runs on Cloudflare, which
      handles requests as its infrastructure provider. The demo audio on the
      home page only loads when you press play.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions go to
      <a href="https://github.com/robin-liquidium/stillmic/issues">
        GitHub issues
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </main>
</Page>
